(c) rebrand, rename, or present ClaimShift or a derivative work as your own software;
(d) sell, sublicense, rent, license, or otherwise commercially distribute ClaimShift itself;
(e) remove or obscure copyright, authorship, license, or attribution notices;
(f) copy substantial portions of ClaimShift source code into another plugin, product, or project;
(g) use the source code to create and distribute a competing or substitute implementation derived from ClaimShift; or
(h) use a contribution-focused fork to publish releases, binaries, packages, or an independently distributed derivative project.

Public GitHub forks are permitted only when they are used for contribution, review, testing, or patch development and remain clearly connected to the original ClaimShift project.

